!Sample_treatment_protocol_ch1 = 5 Mio cells HeLa Tet::Cas9 RelA-mNeonGreen were plated out per 15 cm plate 24 hours before transduction to reach 40-50% confluency at the time point of transduction. 12 plates were transduced with 5 µl 40x concentrated virus in the presence of polybrene per genome-wide sublibrary. For the NFkB focused library, 6 plates were transduced. 24 hours after transduction, cells were collected and plated out in the same number of plates in the presence of Puromycin (concentrations as above for individual gRNAs). Dead cells were collected 24 h after addition of Puromycin, with maximum cell death occurring until 48 hours after addition of Puromycin. 4 days after transduction, medium was changed again and cells were cultivated further in the presence of Puromycin and Doxycycline, followed by 7 days without Doxycycline. Cells were split four times during these 2 weeks of cultivation, while 3 Mio cells were plated out per 15 cm plate and the number of plates were adjusted to keep at least 1000x coverage of each sublibrary. On the day of analysis, cells were treated with TNFa and collected as described above. Cells for each sublibrary were prepared in several batches of 2-3 plates, in order not to exceed 2 hours of storage on ice during recording.
!Sample_growth_protocol_ch1 = HeLa cell lines (HeLa Kyoto , HeLa with organelle markers, HeLa Tet::Cas9 RelA-mNeonGreen) were maintained in DMEM (Thermo, 41965039) supplemented with 10% FBS and penicillin–streptomycin (P/S) (Thermo).
!Sample_molecule_ch1 = genomic DNA
!Sample_extract_protocol_ch1 = Genomic DNA was prepared from sorted lower and upper bins and input samples containing 80,000 to 2 Mio cells per sample. Monarch genomic DNA purification kit (New England Biolabs) was used for gDNA preparations while including the RNase treatment. CROP/gRNA loci were amplified from gDNA using a nested PCR strategy with outer primers and barcoded inner primers containing Illumina adapters.
!Sample_extract_protocol_ch1 = Libraries were pooled and sequenced using an Illumina NextSeq 500 in high output mode with 8 reads to read out the i7 barcode, and 67 reads on Read1 to read through the stagger sequence and identify the gRNA. CRISPR guide RNA library sequencing
!Sample_data_processing = gRNA abundance was quantified using mageck count (Mageck v 0.5.9.4)
!Sample_data_processing = Genome_build: hg38
!Sample_data_processing = Supplementary_files_format_and_content: .txt file containing raw gRNA counts were generated using mageck count (Mageck v 0.5.9.4).
!Sample_platform_id = GPL18573
!Sample_contact_name = Benedikt,,Rauscher
!Sample_contact_institute = EMBL
!Sample_contact_address = Meyerhofstr. 1
!Sample_contact_city = Heidelberg
!Sample_contact_zip/postal_code = 69117
!Sample_contact_country = Germany
!Sample_instrument_model = NextSeq 500
!Sample_library_selection = other
!Sample_library_source = genomic
!Sample_library_strategy = OTHER
!Sample_relation = BioSample: https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/biosample/SAMN18093929
!Sample_relation = SRA: https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/sra?term=SRX10194606
!Sample_supplementary_file_1 = ftp://ftp.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/geo/samples/GSM5116nnn/GSM5116012/suppl/GSM5116012_FocusedScreen_lower_160kCells.count.txt.gz
